om2
note enc: page text on stdin becomes an om2 unit on stdout
note the emitted unit holds one text record per input line and its main writes the same bytes back
note exit 0 ok, 2 read error, 3 input of 1000000 bytes or more, 4 control byte refused (below 32 other
note than tab and newline, or 127), 5 over 8000 lines, 6 write error
note out is a reserved word in om2 units so the output pool is ob
note pinned compiler: omc sha256 f4fa7951 (omega-mv b2ad967e seed/out/omc); omc 2c824805 refuses
note this unit (error 8 on the bound 1000000 of slurp). See tools/pageunit/omc.sh.
note
note Unit layout and why 8000 lines. The pinned omc keeps texts and the locals of the function being
note compiled in one table of 8192 names (8192 texts and a bare main compile, 8193 are error 14),
note and refuses a function body of more than 6552 calls (error 14). So the unit puts at most 1000
note calls in each part function p00 .. p07 and main calls the parts; with emit's 4 locals the text
note count may reach 8188, and enc stops at 8000 (exit 5) so every unit it writes compiles.
note
note Output bound (no input traps or overflows ob). Let n < 1000000 be the input bytes and R <= 8000
note the records, P = ceil(R / 1000) <= 8 the parts. Each record costs 14 bytes around its body
note (text t, 4 digits, space quote, quote newline) and 11 bytes for its call (emit t, 4 digits,
note newline); every input byte becomes at most 2 body bytes (quote, backslash, tab and newline are
note escaped as 2, every other accepted byte is copied). Each part costs 15 bytes for its fn line,
note 4 for its end and 4 for its call in main. So
note   size <= C + 2 n + 25 R + 23 P <= C + 1999998 + 200000 + 184 = C + 2200182
note where C = |HEAD| + |EMITA| + |EMITB| + |MAINH| + |TAIL| = 139 + 80 + 71 + 15 + 10 = 315 bytes,
note so size <= 2200497 < 4194304 = |ob|. The input made only of quotes and newlines with 8000
note records reaches the bound exactly (gen w in tests/pageunit: 2200497 bytes).
note Loop bounds: slurp reads at least one byte per pass until it reads 0, at most 1000000 bytes,
note so at most 1000001 passes; flush writes at least one byte per pass of at most |ob| bytes.
global inp uchar 1048576
global ob uchar 4194304
global st ulong 1
text HEAD "om2\nnote cortex page unit generated by tools/pageunit/enc.om\nnote compile with omc f4fa7951 and run: stdout is the page text byte for byte\n"
text TXT "text t"
text QOPEN " \""
text QEND "\"\n"
text EMITA "fn emit a view uchar * to void\nn = len a\no = ulong 0\nwhile lt o n bound 1000000\n"
text EMITB "k = write 1 a o sub n o\nif le k 0\nexit 1\nend\no = add o ulong k\nend\nend\n"
text PARTA "fn p"
text PARTB " to void\n"
text PEND "end\n"
text CALLP "p"
text MAINH "fn main to int\n"
text CALL "emit t"
text NL "\n"
text TAIL "ret 0\nend\n"
fn putb c uchar to void
p = get st 0
put ob p c
put st 0 add p 1
end
fn puts a view uchar * to void
n = len a
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 4096
putb get a i
i = add i 1
end
end
fn digit v ulong d ulong to uchar
q = rem div v d 10
ret uchar add q 48
end
fn putnum v ulong to void
putb digit v 1000
putb digit v 100
putb digit v 10
putb digit v 1
end
fn putpart v ulong to void
putb digit v 10
putb digit v 1
end
fn slurp to long
note every pass reads at least one byte or ends the loop; at most 1000000 bytes are accepted
n = ulong 0
go = ulong 1
err = long 0
while eq go 1 bound 1000001
k = read 0 inp n sub 1000000 n
if lt k 0
err = k
go = ulong 0
else
if eq k 0
go = ulong 0
else
n = add n ulong k
end
end
end
if lt err 0
ret err
end
ret long n
end
fn flush to int
n = get st 0
o = ulong 0
while lt o n bound 4194304
k = write 1 ob o sub n o
if le k 0
ret 6
end
o = add o ulong k
end
ret 0
end
fn calls cnt ulong to void
note part functions of at most 1000 emit calls each, then main calling every part
j = ulong 0
pn = ulong 0
while lt j cnt bound 8000
if eq rem j 1000 0
puts PARTA
putpart pn
puts PARTB
end
puts CALL
putnum j
puts NL
j = add j 1
if eq rem j 1000 0
puts PEND
pn = add pn 1
end
end
if ne rem cnt 1000 0
puts PEND
pn = add pn 1
end
puts MAINH
k = ulong 0
while lt k pn bound 8
puts CALLP
putpart k
puts NL
k = add k 1
end
puts TAIL
end
fn main to int
got = slurp
if lt got 0
ret 2
end
n = ulong got
if ge n 1000000
ret 3
end
puts HEAD
i = ulong 0
cnt = ulong 0
opn = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 1000000
c = get inp i
if eq opn 0
if ge cnt 8000
ret 5
end
puts TXT
putnum cnt
puts QOPEN
opn = ulong 1
end
if eq c 10
putb 92
putb 110
puts QEND
opn = ulong 0
cnt = add cnt 1
else
if eq c 9
putb 92
putb 116
else
if lt c 32
ret 4
end
if eq c 127
ret 4
end
if eq c 34
putb 92
end
if eq c 92
putb 92
end
putb c
end
end
i = add i 1
end
if eq opn 1
puts QEND
cnt = add cnt 1
end
puts EMITA
puts EMITB
calls cnt
ret flush
end
